dbo.StockLst_Process Feild definition
[Process_ID] CHAR(10)

CANCELLED	-Trigger to Delete
RECEIVED	-Trigger to Delete
Sell Stock	-Trigger to Delete
Shipped		-Trigger to Delete
Receiving	-Trigger to Delete

Main Process: 
INCOMING 	-Material is incoming, from PO or WO_Detail 
SELECTED 	-Material has been selected for a SO or WO

CANCELLED	-a way to remove the process when the PO SO WO or WO_Detail is cancelled. -Trigger to Delete
CORRECTION 	-Shop StockLst Edit-Inventory Correction, Bring back deleted StockLst records.

depricate PARTSELECT -a partial Select, may not need to use. Just use SELECTED

NOT2HPA  	-material is incoming but not to HPA, Simulate a Packing slip data
Receiving	-Receive_Edit:Create_Receive_Process()  -Trigger to Delete
depricate PARTRECV -Just use INCOMING 

RECEIVED	-did not find as Process_ID -Trigger to Delete
Sell Stock	-did not find as Process_ID -Trigger to Delete
Shipped		-did not find as Process_ID	-Trigger to Delete
SUBED	 	-did not find as Process_ID


Process_After Trigger to Delete: 'RECEIVED' 'Sell Stock' 'Shipped' 'Receiving' 'CORRECTION' 'CANCELLED'
QTY		-Process QTY Selected
Ordered_QTY -Complete QTY needed for Ordered
Ordered_P	-Price Sold or Purchased at

*******************************************

SELECT DISTINCT H.Process_ID 
,( SELECT COUNT(Process_ID) FROM dbo.[AR.StockLst_Process_History WHERE Process_ID = H.Process_ID ) AS CNTD
FROM dbo.[AR.StockLst_Process_History  H WHERE YEAR(H.[when] ) = 2018  ORDER BY CNTD

